    "physical_description": "Carpet fragment (or small bag face)\r\n\r\nWARP: white wool; Z2S; 21 threads per inch (86 per dm).\r\n\r\nWEFT: light brown and red wool; Z spun, unplied; 2 parallel threads per shoot (one of brown and one of red); 2 shoots after each row of knots; 30 knots per inch (112 per dm).\r\n\r\nPILE: wool; 8 colours: dark red, red, yellow, green, blue, light blue, brown, white; asymmetrical knot open to the right and tied around 2 threads; 315 knots per sq. inch (4816 per sq. dm).\r\n\r\nSIDE FINISH: cut\r\n\r\nEND FINISH: cut\r\n\r\nDESIGN: Field: four white panels, each containing a stylised plant form.  Across the middle of each stem there is a stepped gul.\r\n\r\nBorder: above, below and between these panels (except on the left) there is a red ground border divided into squares and each containing a coloured sprig.\r\n\r\nLowere band: incomplete.\r\n\r\nDate catalogued> 29.6.94",
